// Tests for Vale alerts inside \list blocks.
//
// BUG C — list_block duplicate alerts (Pass 1 + Pass 2):
//   qdocCollectProse recurses into list_block (correct for sentence-scope
//   rules), but Pass 1 already linted the same text nodes via the catch-all.
//   Both passes fire, producing duplicate alerts.

/*!
    \class QLibrary
    \brief Loads a shared library at run-time.

    \list
      \li The library is resolved on first access.
      \li Symbols are exported by the shared object.
      \li The handle is closed when unload() is called.
    \endlist

    The library path is set before the handle is opened.
*/
// Expected (after fixes):
//   16: Microsoft.Passive 'is resolved'             (inside list — BUG C: currently fires twice, at 16+17)
//   17: Microsoft.Passive 'are exported'            (inside list — BUG C: currently fires twice, at 17+19)
//   18: Microsoft.Passive 'is closed', 'is called'  (inside list — BUG C: currently fires twice, at 18+21)
//   21: Microsoft.Passive 'is set', 'is opened'     (post-list — correct already)

// Minimal list test — passive voice in \li items (BUG C: cumulative +N offset per item).

/*!
    \class QNetworkInterface
    \brief Provides a listing of network interfaces.

    \list
      \li The address is assigned by the network manager.
      \li The interface is identified by its hardware address.
      \li The route is selected automatically.
    \endlist

    The interface name is set at initialization.
*/
// Current behavior (BUG C: Pass 1 + Pass 2 both fire, cumulative +N offset per item):
//   36: Microsoft.Passive 'is assigned'   (Pass 1 — correct)
//   37: Microsoft.Passive 'is assigned'   (BUG C dup — Pass 2 offset +1)
//   37: Microsoft.Passive 'is identified' (Pass 1 — correct)
//   38: Microsoft.Passive 'is selected'   (Pass 1 — correct)
//   39: Microsoft.Passive 'is identified' (BUG C dup — Pass 2 offset +2)
//   41: Microsoft.Passive 'is selected'   (BUG C dup — Pass 2 offset +3)
//   41: Microsoft.Passive 'is set'        (post-list — correct, no dup)
// Expected (after fix — one alert per passive, correct lines):
//   36: Microsoft.Passive 'is assigned'
//   37: Microsoft.Passive 'is identified'
//   38: Microsoft.Passive 'is selected'
//   41: Microsoft.Passive 'is set'
